---
/**
 * Publishes the poll-of-polls data bundle to `window.__POP_DATA__` so the
 * interactive widget embedded in the blog post can read it.
 *
 * The data itself is generated by the Python pipeline in
 * `analysis/nfl-power-rankings/` (`python3 run.py`), which writes
 * `src/data/nfl-power-rankings-latest.json`. The post renders from that file
 * at build time, so the page stays a static artifact and no runtime fetch or
 * Python dependency is needed to build the site.
 *
 * The payload is injected with `is:inline` because it must execute before the
 * widget's own inline script, which Astro has already hoisted into the head.
 */
import bundle from '../data/nfl-power-rankings-latest.json';
---

<script is:inline set:html={`window.__POP_DATA__ = ${JSON.stringify(bundle)};`} />
